1
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:08,960
Why hast thou forsaken me, O deity whose existence I doubt?

2
00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:13,290
Here. Breathe into this bag.

3
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:15,760
What's going on?

4
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:18,430
They stole everything, Leonard!

5
00:00:18,430 --> 00:00:19,900
Everything.

6
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:21,630
Are you the roommate?

7
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,700
Yeah, Leonard Hofstadter. What happened?

8
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,940
Your friend here called 911 to report a robbery.

9
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:27,870
Oh, my God, what did they get?

10
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:29,180
What didn't they get?

11
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:31,110
They got my enchanted weapons,

12
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:33,080
my vicious gladiator armor,

13
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:35,420
my wand of untainted power,

14
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:37,980
and all my gold!

15
00:00:38,390 --> 00:00:40,190
You called the police

16
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:42,990
because someone hacked your World of Warcraft account?

17
00:00:42,990 --> 00:00:45,430
What choice did I have?

18
00:00:45,430 --> 00:00:48,590
The mighty Sheldor, level 85 blood elf,

19
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:50,400
hero of the Eastern kingdoms,

20
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:54,600
has been picked clean, like a carcass in the desert sun.

21
00:00:55,870 --> 00:00:57,600
Plus, the FBI hung up on me.

22
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:02,110
Into the bag.

23
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:05,410
They took my battle ostrich!

24
00:01:05,410 --> 00:01:07,750
- Oh, no, not Glenn! - Yes!

25
00:01:07,750 --> 00:01:09,120
Glenn!

26
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:11,280
The only bird I ever loved.

27
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:14,590
Good luck, fellas.

28
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:16,290
Oh. Well, thank you, officer.

29
00:01:16,290 --> 00:01:17,560
Wait a minute!

30
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:19,060
You're not going to do anything?

31
00:01:19,060 --> 00:01:20,230
Mr. Cooper, there's nothing...

32
00:01:20,230 --> 00:01:21,730
Dr. Cooper.

33
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:24,300
Seriously?

34
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:28,170
Not the kind with access to drugs.

35
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:31,140
Fine. Dr. Cooper.

36
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:32,570
I'm sorry for your loss,

37
00:01:32,570 --> 00:01:34,110
but the Pasadena Police Department

38
00:01:34,110 --> 00:01:36,340
doesn't have jurisdiction in...

39
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:38,240
Pandora.

40
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:40,910
That's from Avatar

41
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:44,250
World of Warcraft takes place in Azeroth.

42
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:47,120
Goodness gracious, how are you allowed to carry a gun?

43
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:52,260
Can you at least refer me to a rogue ex-cop?

44
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:53,590
What?

45
00:01:53,590 --> 00:01:56,400
Wh-- you know, one who was drummed off the force

46
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,230
because he refused to play by the rules,

47
00:01:58,230 --> 00:01:59,930
and now he hires himself out

48
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:03,140
to impose his own brand of rough justice?

49
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,870
No.

50
00:02:07,270 --> 00:02:08,940
Thank you, officer.

51
00:02:09,810 --> 00:02:12,450
It's all gone. All gone.

52
00:02:12,450 --> 00:02:14,310
I'm really sorry, Sheldon.

53
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:15,980
What kind of world do we live in,

54
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:19,950
where a man would take another man's battle ostrich?

55
00:02:19,950 --> 00:02:21,820
I don't know.

56
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:24,190
This act of aggression must be met

57
00:02:24,190 --> 00:02:26,560
with swift and cruel ferocity.

58
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:31,200
It is time to cry havoc, and let slip the dogs of war.

59
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,370
I'm on it.

60
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:39,470
Hi, Mrs. Wolowitz. Is, is Howard there?

61
00:02:40,770 --> 00:02:42,640
Okay, thanks.

62
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,140
That particular dog of war

63
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:46,250
will have to call you back after his bath.

64
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:52,180
See if Raj is done with Pilates.

65
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:19,360
Three thousand hours.

66
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:22,500
Three thousand hours clicking on that mouse,

67
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:24,470
collecting weapons and gold.

68
00:03:24,470 --> 00:03:29,370
It's almost as if it was a huge waste of time.

69
00:03:29,370 --> 00:03:30,970
Whoever did this knew what they were doing.

70
00:03:30,970 --> 00:03:33,010
He got in and out of your account in under

71
00:03:33,010 --> 00:03:35,510
15 minutes, transferred all your stuff,

72
00:03:35,510 --> 00:03:36,740
and didn't leave a digital fingerprint.

73
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:38,010
Oh!

74
00:03:38,010 --> 00:03:40,550
There isn't enough chamomile tea in the world

75
00:03:40,550 --> 00:03:43,450
to quell the rage in my heart.

76
00:03:44,590 --> 00:03:46,150
Hold on. I'm talking to an orc

77
00:03:46,150 --> 00:03:47,720
under the bridge in Thunder Bluff

78
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:50,560
who says if we pay him, he'll help us track down your things.

79
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:52,060
Can we trust him?

80
00:03:52,060 --> 00:03:54,390
I should say so; he appears to be a member

81
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:56,900
of the Nigerian royal family.

82
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:01,270
Whoa! Somebody's auctioning off a jeweled ostrich bridle!

83
00:04:01,270 --> 00:04:03,400
No. Glenn's was leather.

84
00:04:04,270 --> 00:04:06,440
He was a simple ostrich.

85
00:04:06,440 --> 00:04:09,440
Is! Is, I haven't given up hope.

86
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:12,210
Hey.

87
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:14,450
Hey, Penny. We're kind of in the middle of a crisis, here.

88
00:04:14,450 --> 00:04:16,820
Oh, I know. Bernadette told me.

89
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:20,150
Sorry, Sheldon. I know that game meant a lot to you.

90
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,220
What-- "that game"?

91
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:27,160
Excuse me, Penny, but Doodle Jump is a game.

92
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:29,830
Angry Birds is a game.

93
00:04:29,830 --> 00:04:31,330
World of Warcraft is a

94
00:04:31,330 --> 00:04:35,470
massively multi-player online role-playing...

95
00:04:35,470 --> 00:04:37,400
all right, technically it's a game.

96
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:43,870
Bad news, the Nigerian prince may be a fraud.

97
00:04:43,870 --> 00:04:46,110
Okay, well, anyways, I brought you

98
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:47,680
a day-old cheesecake to cheer you up!

99
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:50,250
Stale pastry is hollow succor

100
00:04:50,250 --> 00:04:52,720
to a man who is bereft of ostrich.

101
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:55,020
Just say "thank you".

102
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:57,590
I thought I just did.

103
00:04:57,590 --> 00:05:01,420
All right. See you later.

104
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:02,520
Oh! Hello.

105
00:05:02,530 --> 00:05:02,900
Oh, hi!

106
00:05:02,910 --> 00:05:05,570
I was just dropping off a cheesecake to Sheldon.

107
00:05:05,570 --> 00:05:07,960
He was robbed of a bunch of imaginary crap

108
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:10,530
that's useful in a make-believe place.

109
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:12,870
I don't know what that means.

110
00:05:12,870 --> 00:05:15,700
Yeah, well, sadly, I do.

111
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:20,010
Did you know last weekend Priya took Leonard

112
00:05:20,010 --> 00:05:21,410
rollerblading at the beach?

113
00:05:21,410 --> 00:05:23,180
Can you believe that?

114
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:26,150
I feel like I'm supposed to say "that bitch",

115
00:05:26,150 --> 00:05:28,680
but I don't have enough information.

116
00:05:28,690 --> 00:05:31,050
I am the one who spent two years

117
00:05:31,050 --> 00:05:32,290
trying to get him to even

118
00:05:32,290 --> 00:05:33,890
go to the beach in the first place.

119
00:05:33,890 --> 00:05:35,960
And he was so phobic about stepping on medical waste,

120
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:37,860
I had to carry him to the water.

121
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:40,560
I took Howard to the beach once.

122
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:43,630
He almost burst into flames like a vampire.

123
00:05:44,730 --> 00:05:47,800
So what's the thanks I get for turning Leonard

124
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,510
into quality boyfriend material?

125
00:05:49,510 --> 00:05:51,670
I have to tiptoe around his new girlfriend.

126
00:05:51,670 --> 00:05:54,340
I think you're on.

127
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:57,610
That bitch!

128
00:05:57,610 --> 00:06:00,350
Want some coffee liqueur on your ice cream?

129
00:06:00,350 --> 00:06:03,250
Ah, here's the alcohol and drug peer pressure

130
00:06:03,250 --> 00:06:04,750
Mother warned me about.

131
00:06:05,150 --> 00:06:08,590
I was starting to think it was never going to happen.

132
00:06:08,590 --> 00:06:11,330
Yes, please.

133
00:06:11,330 --> 00:06:13,030
You guys should've seen Leonard when I first met him.

134
00:06:13,030 --> 00:06:14,030
There was no eye contact.

135
00:06:14,030 --> 00:06:15,430
He was either looking up at the ceiling,

136
00:06:15,430 --> 00:06:17,100
or down at his shoes.

137
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:19,030
I'm drunk.

138
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:22,840
You know, for the first couple of months,

139
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,640
whenever I would take off my bra,

140
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:29,480
he would giggle and say, "Oh, boy, my breast friends"!

141
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:31,750
Well, if it makes you feel any better,

142
00:06:31,750 --> 00:06:33,720
I'm never speaking to Priya again.

143
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,750
No, don't do that.

144
00:06:34,750 --> 00:06:36,320
No reason to be mean to her.

145
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:39,720
This may be the alcohol talking...

146
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:40,990
but I believe there is.

147
00:06:40,990 --> 00:06:43,130
Are you familiar with the recent study

148
00:06:43,130 --> 00:06:45,560
of Tanzanian chimpanzees by Nishida and Hosaka

149
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:47,800
out of Kyoto University?

150
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:51,030
No, but I can name all the Kardashians.

151
00:06:51,030 --> 00:06:53,940
Primates, such as ourselves, have a natural instinct

152
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:56,570
to ostracize ill-mannered members of the troop.

153
00:06:56,570 --> 00:06:57,910
Bernadette's urge to

154
00:06:57,910 --> 00:07:00,710
shun, scowl or fling her waste at Priya

155
00:07:00,710 --> 00:07:02,950
is hard-wired into her DNA.

156
00:07:02,950 --> 00:07:06,850
I don't have an urge to fling my waste.

157
00:07:06,850 --> 00:07:09,220
Believe me, it's there, we all have it.

158
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:12,350
Hit me with some more booze, and I'll show you.

159
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:16,830
All right, here we are -- this is the tavern

160
00:07:16,830 --> 00:07:20,460
where all the black-market weapon trades go down.

161
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:23,270
I don't think my character should be in a place like this.

162
00:07:23,270 --> 00:07:25,470
Everyone's undressing her with their eyes.

163
00:07:25,470 --> 00:07:27,640
Maybe if you stop dropping your sword

164
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,870
and bending over to pick it up.

165
00:07:31,310 --> 00:07:32,980
Okay, what exactly are we looking for?

166
00:07:32,980 --> 00:07:35,010
Redheaded troll, goes by the name of Glumly.

167
00:07:35,010 --> 00:07:36,040
According to the message boards,

168
00:07:36,050 --> 00:07:37,580
if you want to move stolen goods

169
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:39,720
and it's after school hours, he's your guy.

170
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:42,240
Leonard, is this going to take much longer?

171
00:07:42,240 --> 00:07:44,220
I thought we were going to spend some time together.

172
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:45,650
Uh, we are. In the meantime,

173
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:48,420
you're welcome to whip up a quick character and join us.

174
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:49,990
Seriously?

175
00:07:49,990 --> 00:07:52,590
Well, you have to put in a credit card number,

176
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:54,560
but it's fun.

177
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:56,330
Maybe I should just go home.

178
00:07:56,330 --> 00:07:57,830
Our troll just walked in! I got him!

179
00:07:57,830 --> 00:07:59,670
We got him. We're almost done.

180
00:07:59,670 --> 00:08:01,970
So, how do you guys want to play this?

181
00:08:01,970 --> 00:08:03,510
Be ruthless. You tell him

182
00:08:03,510 --> 00:08:05,810
if he doesn't start talking, we'll register a complaint

183
00:08:05,810 --> 00:08:08,740
with his Internet service provider.

184
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:11,130
Sheldon,what if he gets his Internet

185
00:08:11,130 --> 00:08:12,180
from his cable company?

186
00:08:12,180 --> 00:08:12,740
He could lose his HBO

187
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:17,120
and all their delightful original programming.

188
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:20,490
I don't care! I'm losin' it, man!

189
00:08:20,490 --> 00:08:21,920
Why don't we play this smart?

190
00:08:21,930 --> 00:08:24,230
Try a little "good goblin, bad goblin."

191
00:08:24,230 --> 00:08:26,300
Oh, dear Lord.

192
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:28,560
Nah, I think we have to be more subtle.

193
00:08:28,570 --> 00:08:31,530
Okay, I see where this is going.

194
00:08:31,530 --> 00:08:34,100
Fine, I'll have sex with him.

195
00:08:36,010 --> 00:08:39,210
That's not where it was going.

196
00:08:39,210 --> 00:08:42,440
Good, because I would hate that.

197
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:47,420
Leonard, you're busy-- let's talk tomorrow.

198
00:08:47,420 --> 00:08:49,120
Oh, wait. Hang on. Are you upset?

199
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:52,520
No, no, I think it's sexy to date a boy trapped in a man's body.

200
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:54,220
Good, good.

201
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:57,260
I'll tell you what happens.

202
00:08:58,390 --> 00:09:01,130
And people think I don't get sarcasm.

203
00:09:04,270 --> 00:09:07,270
Well, well, well.

204
00:09:08,570 --> 00:09:09,840
Look who it is.

205
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:10,910
Okay, be nice.

206
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:12,110
Hello.

207
00:09:12,110 --> 00:09:14,040
Hi. We're just heading out for a drink.

208
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:17,050
Because I do that now.

209
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:19,080
Count your blessings

210
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:21,250
you're not a Tanzanian chimp.

211
00:09:22,390 --> 00:09:23,420
What?

212
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:24,390
Don't listen to her--

213
00:09:24,390 --> 00:09:26,290
she's had a lot of ice cream.

214
00:09:26,990 --> 00:09:28,220
Do you want to join us?

215
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:30,890
Oh, thank you, but I have work to do.

216
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,460
Four women walk down the stairs--

217
00:09:35,470 --> 00:09:38,070
how many reach the lobby?

218
00:09:43,310 --> 00:09:45,950
Did your sister say anything when you got home last night?

219
00:09:45,950 --> 00:09:47,890
Oh, no, don't put me in the middle of this.

220
00:09:47,890 --> 00:09:49,550
I'm not going to be your go-between.

221
00:09:49,550 --> 00:09:50,720
Come on, help me out.

222
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:52,120
Am I in trouble?

223
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:54,090
There's no reason to worry.

224
00:09:54,090 --> 00:09:55,230
That's a relief.

225
00:09:55,630 --> 00:09:56,530
I'm sure many women

226
00:09:56,530 --> 00:09:58,760
in happy relationships spend their nights

227
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:01,160
Skyping with their ex-boyfriend Sanjay.

228
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:06,040
Good news, gentlemen-- I found our hacker.

229
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:07,370
What? Really?

230
00:10:07,370 --> 00:10:09,240
Yeah. No one can hide from me,

231
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,940
not Waldo, not Carmen San Diego,

232
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:13,140
not even topless Natalie Portman.

233
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:15,980
I've never said these words before,

234
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:18,380
but good job, Howard!

235
00:10:19,450 --> 00:10:23,920
Thanks. Our culprit is one Mr. Todd Zarnecki,

236
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:25,090
2711 Ocean View Road,

237
00:10:25,090 --> 00:10:26,660
Carlsbad, California.

238
00:10:26,660 --> 00:10:29,660
The name and the address drip with evil.

239
00:10:29,660 --> 00:10:31,000
What else do we know about him?

240
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,830
Why, quite a bit, actually.

241
00:10:32,830 --> 00:10:36,030
I'll bet he's some loser who lives with his parents.

242
00:10:40,570 --> 00:10:43,210
Yes, he does live with his parents.

243
00:10:43,210 --> 00:10:47,510
Here's a Google Earth shot of their house.

244
00:10:47,510 --> 00:10:49,480
Excellent! It's in a cul-de-sac.

245
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:50,650
We can box him in.

246
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:53,580
Hold on, you're thinking of going there?

247
00:10:53,590 --> 00:10:55,890
Carlsbad is only a couple of hours away.

248
00:10:55,890 --> 00:10:57,020
Fine.

249
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:58,960
You walk up to the house, knock on the door

250
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,960
and demand your stuff back. What if he says no?

251
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:03,190
I don't know if you've been following the news, Leonard,

252
00:11:03,190 --> 00:11:05,030
but there have been some terrific advancements

253
00:11:05,030 --> 00:11:06,600
in the field of torture.

254
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:10,070
No one's getting tortured.

255
00:11:10,070 --> 00:11:12,300
Fine, we'll abide by the Geneva Convention.

256
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:13,740
But ask yourself this:

257
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:15,770
in the course of our lives,

258
00:11:15,770 --> 00:11:18,110
how much lunch money has been taken from us?

259
00:11:18,110 --> 00:11:19,880
How many kites?

260
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:22,610
How many Scooby-Doo Trapper Keepers?

261
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:24,750
I totally had one of those.

262
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:26,150
Of course you did.

263
00:11:26,150 --> 00:11:28,690
It was a fun and practical way of organizing your school work.

264
00:11:28,690 --> 00:11:31,060
But the bullies took it from us.

265
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:32,020
Well, no more.

266
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:34,190
Tonight, we take back our dignity,

267
00:11:34,190 --> 00:11:36,290
our birthright and our pride.

268
00:11:36,290 --> 00:11:37,460
What do you say?

269
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:38,960
Who's with me?

270
00:11:43,070 --> 00:11:46,840
I have a hip-hop aerobics class at 5:00; could we go after?

271
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:49,310
Sure.

272
00:11:49,340 --> 00:11:50,370
Also, tonight's the Sabbath

273
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:51,940
and my mother and I have a tradition of

274
00:11:51,940 --> 00:11:54,150
lighting the candles and watching Wheel of Fortune, so...

275
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:55,180
If we could leave at 8:00,

276
00:11:55,180 --> 00:11:56,480
we'd still be able to

277
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:58,080
regain our birthright at 10:00, 10:30 latest.

278
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:00,180
Fine.

279
00:12:00,190 --> 00:12:02,490
Leonard?

280
00:12:02,490 --> 00:12:05,190
Oh, geez, I-I don't know if I can ditch Priya

281
00:12:05,190 --> 00:12:06,490
two nights in a row.

282
00:12:06,490 --> 00:12:07,660
Oh, come on, man.

283
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:10,330
Bros before...

284
00:12:13,670 --> 00:12:15,230
...my sister.

285
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:17,470
Aw, screw it.

286
00:12:17,470 --> 00:12:18,570
- I'm in. - Me, too.

287
00:12:18,570 --> 00:12:20,440
And me.

288
00:12:21,270 --> 00:12:23,470
One moment.

289
00:12:26,950 --> 00:12:29,210
I'm hell-bent on catching a cyber criminal,

290
00:12:29,210 --> 00:12:31,450
not the common cold.

291
00:12:35,820 --> 00:12:37,620
I'm sorry, I thought this delay was

292
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:39,920
so you could watch Wheel of Fortune with your mother.

293
00:12:39,930 --> 00:12:41,190
I am.

294
00:12:41,190 --> 00:12:42,790
She's just bleaching her mustache.

295
00:12:43,660 --> 00:12:45,000
Check it out.

296
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,160
Hey, Ma! "Before and After!"

297
00:12:47,170 --> 00:12:50,600
Four words, 17 letters, two N's, one V!

298
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:53,040
"Fanny pack of wolves!"

299
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,510
That's incredible.

300
00:12:56,510 --> 00:12:58,180
Yeah, she's kind of a Wheel savant.

301
00:12:59,810 --> 00:13:02,410
Uh-oh, that's Priya.

302
00:13:03,550 --> 00:13:07,080
Sitar music for her ringtone is not cool, dude.

303
00:13:07,090 --> 00:13:08,750
Hit the...

304
00:13:09,750 --> 00:13:12,620
Hey, sweetie.

305
00:13:12,620 --> 00:13:13,890
Yeah, I'm sorry.

306
00:13:13,890 --> 00:13:15,790
I'm gonna be working late.

307
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:19,100
Yeah, I-I miss you, too.

308
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:22,100
Okay, sure, I'll call you when I get home.

309
00:13:22,100 --> 00:13:23,600
Okay, bye-bye.

310
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:24,870
Very nice.

311
00:13:24,870 --> 00:13:26,670
You lie to my sister.

312
00:13:28,010 --> 00:13:30,270
That's the nicest thing he does to your sister.

313
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:39,120
Oh, guess who.

314
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:40,650
Cover for me.

315
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:43,990
Hello, Priya. What's up?

316
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:46,360
How would I know if Leonard's at work or not?

317
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:48,890
Don't be suspicious.

318
00:13:48,890 --> 00:13:50,660
Look, if you want your relationship with Leonard

319
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:52,330
to continue, you're going to have to believe

320
00:13:52,330 --> 00:13:54,130
whatever wild-eyed, cockamamie excuse

321
00:13:54,130 --> 00:13:56,330
the white devil has the nerve to offer you.

322
00:13:58,140 --> 00:14:01,070
Okay? Yeah, bye-bye.

323
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:03,910
You owe me.

324
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:06,680
New puzzle, Ma!

325
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:07,950
"Same name"!

326
00:14:07,950 --> 00:14:09,650
One N, two D's, three O's!

327
00:14:09,650 --> 00:14:12,350
Whoopi and Rube Goldberg!

328
00:14:12,350 --> 00:14:13,680
That's uncanny.

329
00:14:13,690 --> 00:14:15,520
I know. It's her superpower.

330
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:17,590
Well, that and jiggling her arm fat.

331
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:23,090
I can't believe we're going all the way to San Diego

332
00:14:23,090 --> 00:14:24,900
to confront this guy.

333
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:27,500
Yeah, we're kind of bad-asses, aren't we?

334
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:28,870
Totally.

335
00:14:28,870 --> 00:14:30,330
Hey, how about we stay the night

336
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:32,800
and hit Legoland in the morning?

337
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,410
Sea World is better.

338
00:14:34,410 --> 00:14:38,440
It has Shamu, who is literally tons of fun.

339
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:41,750
But for the moment, let's stay focused on Todd Zarnecki.

340
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:44,380
Yeah, we're coming for you, Todd Zarnecki.

341
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:47,890
And for the record, Legoland is more interactive.

342
00:14:48,950 --> 00:14:51,250
I almost feel sorry for the poor fool,

343
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:53,960
sitting in his split-level suburban ranch,

344
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:56,190
unaware that a vengeful horde

345
00:14:56,190 --> 00:14:59,000
is barreling down the San Diego Freeway

346
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,230
at 71 miles an hour.

347
00:15:01,230 --> 00:15:02,700
Ease up there, lead foot.

348
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:04,170
You trying to get us killed?

349
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:08,410
I took the liberty of burning us

350
00:15:08,410 --> 00:15:10,510
a mix of heroic questing music.

351
00:15:12,010 --> 00:15:15,780
This says "Beyonce Bootylicious Dance Mix."

352
00:15:15,780 --> 00:15:17,480
It's a re-writable CD.

353
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:19,380
Just put it in.

354
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:21,120
Beyonce? Really?

355
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:22,950
She's curvy and she owns it.

356
00:15:22,950 --> 00:15:24,490
I like that.

357
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:34,900
Oh, yeah, I'm feeling it.

358
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:37,730
We are winged fury!

359
00:15:37,740 --> 00:15:39,140
Which is still no excuse

360
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:41,040
for going over the posted speed limit.

361
00:15:46,510 --> 00:15:48,550
Next time we go to kick someone's ass,

362
00:15:48,550 --> 00:15:50,150
we take the train.

363
00:15:50,150 --> 00:15:53,080
I always prefer the train.

364
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,260
Sheldon, let's go.

365
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,530
Coming.

366
00:16:01,530 --> 00:16:03,370
Why did you bring that?

367
00:16:03,370 --> 00:16:06,400
No weapon strikes more fear into a man's heart

368
00:16:06,410 --> 00:16:08,410
than a Klingon bat'leth.

369
00:16:08,410 --> 00:16:11,580
Okay, let's get clear on something.

370
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:13,650
We're just going to tell this guy to transfer all of

371
00:16:13,650 --> 00:16:16,480
your stuff back into your account and then be on our way.

372
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:18,980
No one's bat'lething anybody.

373
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:22,850
So my blade shall not taste blood tonight?

374
00:16:23,860 --> 00:16:26,390
No.

375
00:16:26,390 --> 00:16:30,030
Well, now I just feel silly holding it.

376
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:31,700
Come on.

377
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:34,000
Can I at least kick down the door?

378
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:34,970
You're welcome to try, but the other day,

379
00:16:34,970 --> 00:16:38,700
it took you 15 minutes to get into a FedEx box.

380
00:16:41,970 --> 00:16:43,140
Who is it?

381
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:44,940
Your doom!

382
00:16:44,940 --> 00:16:46,240
Don't say "your doom."

383
00:16:46,250 --> 00:16:48,650
Who opens the door for their doom?

384
00:16:48,650 --> 00:16:50,020
Good point.

385
00:16:50,020 --> 00:16:52,020
Basket of puppies.

386
00:16:54,620 --> 00:16:55,750
What?

387
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:57,420
Uh...

388
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:00,290
Sheldon?

389
00:17:02,090 --> 00:17:04,460
Are you Todd Zarnecki?

390
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:06,130
Yeah. Who are you?

391
00:17:06,130 --> 00:17:08,300
I am Sheldor of Azeroth.

392
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:09,940
I want my things back.

393
00:17:09,940 --> 00:17:11,070
I don't think so.

394
00:17:11,070 --> 00:17:12,270
Let me see that.

395
00:17:12,270 --> 00:17:13,570
Careful. That's a collectible.

396
00:17:13,570 --> 00:17:14,670
I know.

397
00:17:14,670 --> 00:17:17,740
I've always wanted one.

398
00:17:25,350 --> 00:17:28,450
Well, he's even more cunning than we thought.

399
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:35,870
You know, the joke's on him.

400
00:17:35,870 --> 00:17:38,200
Without the certificate of authenticity,

401
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:40,840
that bat'leth is worthless.

402
00:17:41,240 --> 00:17:44,510
Yeah, he walked right into our trap.

403
00:17:45,780 --> 00:17:49,480
Legoland seems like a hollow dream now.

404
00:17:50,650 --> 00:17:53,050
Uh-oh.

405
00:17:53,050 --> 00:17:54,790
- What's the matter? - Something's wrong.

406
00:17:54,790 --> 00:17:56,390
I'm not getting any gas.

407
00:18:02,730 --> 00:18:05,860
Anybody know anything about internal combustion engines?

408
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:06,860
Of course.

409
00:18:06,860 --> 00:18:08,370
- 19th-century technology. - Very basic.

410
00:18:08,370 --> 00:18:10,700
Does anybody know how to fix an internal combustion engine?

411
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:13,140
- No. - No. - Not a clue.

412
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:16,270
Well, we'd better call somebody to come pick us up.

413
00:18:16,270 --> 00:18:19,140
It'd be swell if they had a train.

414
00:18:24,250 --> 00:18:26,050
Thank you, Penny.

415
00:18:26,350 --> 00:18:28,320
No problem.

416
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:29,850
So, Leonard,

417
00:18:29,850 --> 00:18:31,920
I think it's interesting you didn't call your girlfriend

418
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:33,120
to come get you.

419
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:35,590
Uh, I kind of told her I was working.

420
00:18:35,590 --> 00:18:37,430
So you lied to her.

421
00:18:37,430 --> 00:18:39,300
Also interesting.

422
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:40,870
Yeah, she doesn't really understand

423
00:18:40,870 --> 00:18:44,130
the whole Warcraft adventure-role-playing thing.

424
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:47,770
Well, doesn't matter if she gets it, as long as she's pretty.

425
00:18:48,940 --> 00:18:51,440
This one's funny, Leonard.

426
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:53,880
How come you couldn't make it work with her?

427
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:57,650
So did you at least get Sheldon's fake stuff back?

428
00:18:57,650 --> 00:19:00,950
No. We failed in our noble quest.

429
00:19:00,950 --> 00:19:02,020
How come?

430
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:05,560
Todd Zarnecki was mean.

431
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:07,090
All right. Hang on.

432
00:19:07,090 --> 00:19:08,530
What are you doing?

433
00:19:08,530 --> 00:19:11,560
I'm gonna show you how we finish a quest in Nebraska.

434
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:16,270
Oh. Beyonce.

435
00:19:23,270 --> 00:19:25,080
This ain't no Beyonce.

436
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,670
Now what?

437
00:19:32,010 --> 00:19:33,670
Give my friend his stuff back.

438
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:35,540
I don't know what you're talking about.

439
00:19:35,540 --> 00:19:37,010
Well, then, good news.

440
00:19:37,010 --> 00:19:39,050
Today's the day a girl's finally going to touch you

441
00:19:39,050 --> 00:19:40,450
in your little special place.

442
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:46,220
Now give him his stuff back.

443
00:19:46,220 --> 00:19:47,760
Okay.

444
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:49,220
We did it!

445
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:53,660
I said, "we."

446
00:20:00,170 --> 00:20:02,340
Oh, hold the door.

447
00:20:02,340 --> 00:20:04,010
- Oh, hi. - Hi.

448
00:20:05,170 --> 00:20:06,410
Going to see Leonard?

449
00:20:06,410 --> 00:20:07,410
Yes.

450
00:20:08,710 --> 00:20:09,750
How have you been?

451
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:11,110
Fine. You?

452
00:20:11,110 --> 00:20:13,320
Very well, thank you.

453
00:20:52,690 --> 00:20:54,620
All right, well, great seeing you.

454
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:56,830
Yeah. You, too.

455
00:20:58,290 --> 00:21:00,300
Amy's right.

456
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:03,070
I do want to fling my poop at her.

